Z||000008||Old Lar||09-26-2001||03:09 PM||||Fran Passuite created the Indy Pace Car.  It started it life as an 84 Pace car and Fran redesigned it. He had it professionally constructed. It has a Miller Woods turbo on the 1986 2.8 engine. 17 inch wheels, Koni shocks, lowered, lots of chrome in the engine bay, 5 speed transmission 160 mph speedometer.<P>This car was on the first color cover of "Smoke Signals" many moons ago, and Fran keeps modifying the car i.e. the Lamborghini mirrors, last year.<P>Fran is planning to join the computer age sometime this year, so doesn't post.||||reg||1
Z||000009||chester||09-26-2001||03:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Old Lar:<BR><B>Fran Passuite created the Indy Pace Car.  It started it life as an 84 Pace car and Fran redesigned it. He had it professionally constructed. It has a Miller Woods turbo on the 1986 2.8 engine. 17 inch wheels, Koni shocks, lowered, lots of chrome in the engine bay, 5 speed transmission 160 mph speedometer.<P>This car was on the first color cover of "Smoke Signals" many moons ago, and Fran keeps modifying the car i.e. the Lamborghini mirrors, last year.<P>Fran is planning to join the computer age sometime this year, so doesn't post.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah what he said  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif"><P>Rob D.<P>||||reg||1
